===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|en|enm|sound}}, {{m|enm|sund}}, {{m|enm|isund}}, {{m|enm|ȝesund}}, from {{inh|en|ang|sund|t=sound, safe, whole, uninjured, healthy, prosperous}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*sund}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*sundaz|t=healthy}}, merged with synonymous {{inh|en|ang|ġesund}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*gasund}}.

Cognate with {{cog|sco|sound}}, {{m|sco|soun|t=healthy, sound}}, {{cog|stq|suund}}, {{m|stq|gesuund|t=healthy}}, {{cog|fy|sûn|t=healthy}}, {{cog|nl|gezond|t=healthy, sound}}, {{cog|nds|sund}}, {{m|nds|gesund|t=healthy}}, {{cog|de|gesund|t=healthy, sound}}, {{cog|da|sund|t=healthy}}, {{cog|sv|sund|t=sound, healthy}}. Possibly related also to {{cog|nl|gezwind|t=fast, quick}}, {{cog|de|geschwind|t=fast, quick}}, {{cog|ang|swīþ|t=strong, mighty, powerful, active, severe, violent}}. See {{m|en|swith}}.

====Adjective====
{{en-adj|er}}

# [[healthy|Healthy]].
#: {{ux|en|He was safe and '''sound'''.}}
#: {{ux|en|In horse management a '''sound''' horse is one with no health problems that might affect its suitability for its intended work.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|editor=[[w:Montague Chambers|Montagu[e] Chambers]]|chapter=Roscorla v. Thomas|title=The Law Journal Reports for the Year 1842|location=London|publisher=E. B. Ince, 5 Quality Court, {{w|Chancery Lane}}|date=30 May 1842|volume=XX (New Series – volume XI, part II)|pages=214–215|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=AY4sAQAAMAAJ&pg=PA214|oclc=124015025|passage=on the 29th of September 1840, in consideration that the plaintiff, at the request of the defendant, had bought of the defendant a certain horse, at a certain price, to wit, 30''l.'', the defendant promised plaintiff that the horse did not exceed five years off, and that it was '''sound''' in wind and limb, perfect in vision, and free from vice; {{...}}}}
# [[complete|Complete]], [[solid]], or [[secure]].
#: {{ux|en|Fred assured me the floorboards were '''sound'''.}}
#* {{RQ:Homer Chapman Odysseys|year=1857|passage=The brasswork here, how rich it is in beams, / And how, besides, it makes the whole house '''sound'''.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2021 November 17|author=Andrew Mourant|title=Okehampton: a new dawn for Dartmoor|journal=Rail|issue=944|page=43|text=Refurbishing Okehampton station, kept basically '''sound''' under ownership by Devon Council, remains a work in progress and scheduled for completion next spring.}}
# {{lb|en|mathematics|logic}} Having the property of [[soundness]].
#: {{hyper|en|valid}}
#* {{RQ:Schuster Hepaticae|volume=V|page=vii|text=With fresh material, taxonomic conclusions are leavened by recognition that the material examined reflects the site it occupied; a herbarium packet gives one only a small fraction of the data desirable for '''sound''' conclusions. Herbarium material does not, indeed, allow one to extrapolate safely: what you see is what you get{{...}}}}
# {{lb|en|British|Irish|slang}} [[good|Good]]; [[acceptable]]; [[decent]].
#: {{ux|en|How are you? —I'm '''sound'''.}}
#: {{ux|en|That's a '''sound''' track you're playing.}}
#: {{ux|en|See that man over there? He's '''sound'''. You should get to know him.}}
# {{lb|en|of sleep}} [[quiet|Quiet]] and [[deep]].
#: {{ux|en|[[sound asleep|'''Sound''' asleep]] means sleeping peacefully, and often deeply.}}
#: {{ux|en|Her sleep was '''sound'''.}}
#: {{ux|en|a '''sound''' night’s sleep}} 
# Heavy; [[laid]] on with [[force]].
#: {{ux|en|a '''sound''' beating}}
# Founded in law; legal; valid; not defective.
